# ==============================================================================
# Example 47: E. coli K-12 MG1655 Genome-Scale Metabolic Model Simulation
# ==============================================================================
#
# This example reconstructs and simulates the metabolism of Escherichia coli
# K-12 MG1655 using the GEM pipeline. All gene sequences are real E. coli
# MG1655 sequences from NCBI RefSeq NC_000913.3.
#
# The pipeline performs:
#   Stage 1: Genome import (protein FASTA with real E. coli sequences)
#   Stage 2: Functional annotation (EC numbers, KEGG KOs)
#   Stage 3: Metabolic network reconstruction (bottom-up + top-down + consensus)
#   Stage 4: GRN inference (TF detection + regulatory interactions)
#   Stage 5: Kinetic parameter estimation (kcat/Km from EC class medians)
#   Stage 6: Gap-filling + Flux Balance Analysis (FBA)
#
# Input: E. coli MG1655 core metabolism proteome (46 real proteins)
#        covering glycolysis, TCA cycle, pentose phosphate, fermentation,
#        anaplerotic reactions, and global transcriptional regulators.
#
# Growth medium: glucose minimal (10 mmol/L glucose, 20 mmol/L O2)
# Expected growth rate: ~0.35 h^-1 (consistent with E. coli in minimal medium)
#
# Reference: Orth et al. (2011) E. coli genome-scale metabolic model.
# ==============================================================================

#gem organism=e_coli_k12 genome=data/ecoli_core_genome.fasta medium=glucose_minimal use_database=true include_spontaneous=true gapfill=true dynamic=true duration=24.0 dt=0.1 expression=true target_organism=Escherichia coli

#config backend=gem ticks=1

#sim output=stage,status,genes_annotated,reactions_total,grn_edges,kcat_predictions,km_estimates
